# Narrowed-replay cache: a machine-generated map from mutation label to the test that catches it.
# Disposable by design — deleting it costs one slow run and nothing else, which is exactly why it is
# not committed. `scripts/mutations.ps1` stays hand-curated; this is not.
scripts/mutation-claims.json  # The mutation runner's crash-recovery scratch copies of the files it is mid-way through editing.
  # Same reasoning as `mutation-claims.json` above: a machine-generated snapshot of a tree that is
  # deliberately broken right now is not source, and committing it captures mutants as if they were
  # the real thing.
  scripts/.mutation-backup